    "raw_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task\": \"Propose a reasonable reproducible usage scenario for probing FMU behavior.\",\n  \"inputs\": [\n    {\"name\": \"mu\", \"description\": \"Nonlinearity parameter affecting the behavior of the oscillator.\"},\n    {\"name\": \"der(x0)\", \"description\": \"Rate of change of the first state, which can be excited with various input signals.\"},\n    {\"name\": \"der(x1)\", \"description\": \"Rate of change of the second state, similar to der(x0), used to investigate oscillator dynamics.\"}\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    {\"name\": \"x0\", \"description\": \"The first state of the Van der Pol oscillator.\"},\n    {\"name\": \"x1\", \"description\": \"The second state of the Van der Pol oscillator.\"},\n    {\"name\": \"der(x0)\", \"description\": \"The rate of change of the first state, useful for probing system dynamics.\"},\n    {\"name\": \"der(x1)\", \"description\": \"The rate of change of the second state, indicating oscillatory behavior.\"},\n    {\"name\": \"mu\", \"description\": \"Fixed parameter controlling the system's nonlinearity, may be varied to test system's stability.\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"This scenario will investigate the Van der Pol oscillator’s response to step, ramp, and sine wave excitations. The input variables will include the nonlinear parameter (mu), and the rate of change of the first and second states (der(x0) and der(x1)). The system will be excited with a step change in mu, a ramp signal for der(x0), and a sine wave for der(x1). The outputs x0, x1, and their rates of change will be recorded to analyze the oscillator’s behavior under varying excitations.\"\n}\n```"
